WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.158
Does saying no end a friendship?

00:00:03.158 --> 00:00:06.316
Reluctant agreement can complicate cooperation.

00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:09.474
Assertiveness guidance focuses on clarity and respect.

00:00:09.474 --> 00:00:12.632
Both people’s needs can be acknowledged.

00:00:12.632 --> 00:00:15.789
Effects depend on relationships and power.

00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:22.105
Name the concrete request.

00:00:22.105 --> 00:00:28.421
State what you can and cannot do.

00:00:28.421 --> 00:00:34.737
Offer a feasible arrangement if you wish.

00:00:34.737 --> 00:00:41.053
This doorway represents a negotiable limit.

00:00:41.053 --> 00:00:44.211
One line cannot solve every relationship problem.

00:00:44.211 --> 00:00:47.368
With threats or control, prioritize safety and support.

00:00:47.368 --> 00:00:50.526
Boundaries are not diagnoses of another person.

00:00:50.526 --> 00:00:56.842
State the limit in the actual situation.

00:00:56.842 --> 00:01:03.158
Offer limited help only if it is feasible.

00:01:03.158 --> 00:01:06.316
Clarity can leave room for another proposal.

00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:09.474
Exhaustion need not prove that you care.

00:01:09.474 --> 00:01:12.632
Real cooperation needs a view of real resources.

00:01:12.632 --> 00:01:15.789
Make the feasible next step a little clearer.
